# The shared lines, Phase 8 session 1 (Docs/Design/84 §33, §14.1): openings and closings, widened. turns.talk (Phase 3)
# gave every talk the moves it needs to open and close; at Phase 7 greet.return had one line, and the pups' and the
# night's farewells were the most-said lines of all ("Bye!", "See you!", "Rest well."). These move lines sit beside
# those, a choice among them: more ways to answer a greeting, to take a preclose, to say goodbye and to answer it, and
# to take a refusal well, by the hour, the band, the speaker's age and temper, and in each dialect through #greet#,
# #farewell#, #bless#, #blessing#, #later#, #no_matter#.
#
# Said in nearly every talk, so short (under six words: never "distinctive", R4 and R5), many alternatives. Who says
# what is mostly plain.grammar's #s8_hello#, #s8_okay#, #s8_bye#, #s8_byeback# and #s8_nevermind#, whose most specific
# entry that holds is said (to friends, to strangers, at dawn, by the cold or the merry), not the rules' criteria: a
# rule's criteria make it outrank every rule with fewer (the tiers, §8.2), so a farewell for friends written as a rule
# would be most of all friends' farewells. Only the pups (whose words are their own) and the night (turns.talk's tier
# already) have rules of their own. Nothing claims the hour unless it tests it (truth.json: "good morning").

## A greeting answered (greet.return answers greet, hail, again.open, kin.open)

rule s8t_greet_back
does greet.return
say #s8_hello#. | #s8_hello#. | #greet#. | And to you. | Hello, #address#.

rule s8t_greet_back2
does greet.return
say #s8_hello#. | #s8_hello#. | Hello. | Ah. #greet#.

rule s8t_greet_again
does greet.return
when conv.move=again.open
say Can't keep away. | Back again, aye. | Me again. | Twice, aye. | Here I am. | #s8_hello#.

rule s8t_greet_kin
does greet.return
when conv.move=kin.open
say Hello, you. | Mm? What is it? | Oh. You. | What now? | I'm here. | #s8_hello#.

rule s8t_greet_young
does greet.return
when self.stage=young
say Hi! | Hello! | Hi there! | Hello, hello! | Hiya!

rule s8t_greet_adolescent
does greet.return
when self.stage=adolescent
say Hey. | Oh. Hi. | All right? | Hello. | Hi.

## A preclose taken (accept_preclose answers preclose)

rule s8t_accept
does accept_preclose
say #s8_okay#. | #s8_okay#. | Off you go. | #bc_fair_enough#

rule s8t_accept2
does accept_preclose
say #s8_okay#. | #s8_okay#. | Right. Me too. | Of course, of course.

## Goodbye (farewell), beside turns.talk's

rule s8t_bye
does farewell
say #s8_bye#. | #s8_bye#. | #farewell#. | Go well, then.

rule s8t_bye2
does farewell
say #s8_bye#. | #s8_bye#. | Till next we meet. | Take care, now.

rule s8t_bye_night
does farewell
when here.time=night|dusk
say Night, then. | Sleep easy. | Mind the dark streets. | Off home, then. | Bed for me. | Till tomorrow, then. | Lock your door. | Off to my bed. | Sleep easy, now. | Warm bed, I hope. | #s8_night#. | #s8_night#. | #s8_night#.

rule s8t_bye_young
does farewell
when self.stage=young
say Got to go! Bye! | Off I go! | Bye-bye! | See you soon! | I'm going now. Bye! | #farewell#! | Bye! Bye! | Bye-bye now! | Gotta run! | See you tomorrow! | I'm off!

rule s8t_bye_adolescent
does farewell
when self.stage=adolescent
say Later. | See you around. | I'm off. | Right, bye. | Catch you later. | #farewell#. | See you, then. | I'll be off.

rule s8t_bye_young3
does farewell
when self.stage=young
say #s8_pupbye# | #s8_pupbye# | #s8_pupbye#

rule s8t_bye_adolescent2
does farewell
when self.stage=adolescent
say #s8_teenbye# | #s8_teenbye# | #s8_teenbye#

## Goodbye answered (farewell.return), beside turns.talk's

rule s8t_return
does farewell.return
say #s8_byeback#. | #s8_byeback#. | #farewell#. | And you.

rule s8t_return2
does farewell.return
say #s8_byeback#. | #s8_byeback#. | Go carefully. | Aye. Go well.

rule s8t_return_night
does farewell.return
when here.time=night|dusk
say Night, then. | Sleep easy. | And you. Sleep easy. | Till tomorrow. | Lock your door. | And you. Bed, now. | Night. Mind the dark. | Warm bed, now. | #s8_nightback#. | #s8_nightback#. | #s8_nightback#.

rule s8t_return_young
does farewell.return
when self.stage=young
say Bye-bye! | See you soon! | Bye! Bye! | Bye for now! | #farewell#! | Bye-bye now! | See you tomorrow! | Yes! Bye! | Bye, bye, bye!

rule s8t_return_adolescent
does farewell.return
when self.stage=adolescent
say Later. | See you around. | Yeah, bye. | Catch you later. | #farewell#. | See you, then.

rule s8t_return_young3
does farewell.return
when self.stage=young
say #s8_pupbyeback# | #s8_pupbyeback# | #s8_pupbyeback#

rule s8t_return_adolescent2
does farewell.return
when self.stage=adolescent
say #s8_teenbye# | #s8_teenbye# | #s8_teenbye#

## A refusal taken well (accept_decline answers decline, refuse, put_off)

rule s8t_accept_decline
does accept_decline
say #s8_nevermind#. | #s8_nevermind#. | #no_matter#. | #no_matter#, then.

rule s8t_accept_decline2
does accept_decline
say #s8_nevermind#. | #bc_fair_enough# | Another day, then. | #s8_nevermind#.
